.TH MENU 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
Menu \- A vertical list of selectable text items with keyboard, gamepad and mouse handling built in: the title screen, pause menu, options, a shop, a level select
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqmenu.h\(dq
.ft B
typedef struct Menu {
  MenuItem items[MENU_MAX_ITEMS];
  int   count, selected;
  float x, y, line_h;      /* line_h 0 = from font */
  float hit_w;             /* clickable width; 0 = 200 */
  Font  font;              /* zero = debug font */
  Color color, color_selected;       /* zero = defaults */
} Menu;
.ft R
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A vertical list of selectable text items with keyboard, gamepad and mouse handling built in: the title screen, pause menu, options, a shop, a level select. Keep one in a scene static, build it in on_enter (menu_init, menu_add..., menu_center), feed it input in handle_input (menu_handle_input) and draw it in render (menu_render). Actions are plain functions taking the Engine, so "Play" is a function that calls engine_replace(e, game_scene()). For items whose text changes (a volume percentage) point the label at a static char buffer you snprintf into.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B items
the entries, in order
.TP
.B count
number of items, up to MENU_MAX_ITEMS (12)
.TP
.B selected
index of the highlighted item; set it to preselect
.TP
.B x
left edge of the label column in logical pixels
.TP
.B y
top of the first item
.TP
.B line_h
vertical distance between items; menu_init sets it from the font (line height + 6); 0 = from font
.TP
.B hit_w
width of the clickable strip per item; 0 = 200. menu_center() sets it to the widest label.
.TP
.B font
font for the labels; a zero Font is the debug font
.TP
.B color
color of unselected items; alpha 0 = default grey
.TP
.B color_selected
color of the highlighted item; alpha 0 = default yellow
.SH MODULE
menu (src/engine/menu/menu.h)
